  "post": {
    "title": "The Geminids peak this weekend \u2014 and the Moon stays out of the way \ud83c\udf20",
    "description": "The Geminids peak late on the night of Sunday 13 December 2026, at 23:52 US East Coast time. The radiant in Gemini is highest around 01:52, and the Moon sets at 20:42, so the sky is dark. Up to 150 meteors an hour is the ideal-sky rate (ZHR); from a town expect far fewer. The Moon passes Saturn on the night of 17\u201318 December, 5.9\u00b0 at closest, and the pair is best seen on Thursday evening.\n\nPositions computed for the US East Coast (40.7\u00b0N, 74\u00b0W) with astronomy-engine; meteor rates from the International Meteor Organization. Narration uses a synthetic voice.",
